<title>GERMANY: West German March adjusted jobless rises 1,000.</title>
<headline>West German March adjusted jobless rises 1,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>				 Mar 97	  Feb 97	   Mar 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    3.127 mln     3.257 mln	2.869 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		3.014 mln     3.013 mln	2.772 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)		+1,000	  -17,000	  n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		10.2 pct	10.6 pct	 9.3 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	210,050	 251,182	  293,903</p>
<p> Vacancies		   313,604	 290,025	  304,667</p>
<p>Change in number in work Jan 97	  Dec 96</p>
<p>				 -83,000	 -25,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
